# The natural A₅ generation bound from the original Hall placement

These modules supply the original Thompson movement and paired-linear source
selection, cubic fixed-center comparisons retaining the central summand,
original alpha placement, characteristic block alternative, intrinsic natural
block and core equality, literal commutator Sylow transport, Cartan-axis
alignment, and the terminal Borel/common-component construction.

The actual Hall entrance now supplies omega-center movement, its exact
H centralizer, and both vanishing fixed centers. The original paired
coordinates, alpha order sixteen and literal Cartan-axis recognition are
proved, as are the HStar natural source and every-cubic fixed-center equality.
The selected H component and its Hall cubic now give compatible natural-four
blocks and a literal original torus axis. Their oriented common component has
incompatible cubic-rank bounds, proving generation at most one. The final
weak-closure consumer contradicts generation two using the same actual Hall
placement in the original local join. Chosen quotient irreducibility,
crossed-factor centralization, point-centralizer control and Hall placement
remain the earlier source inputs; no block, axis or generation premise remains.
Source: Aschbacher–Smith 10.2.3(4), pp.746–747.
-/
